WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.035
-Hey, Kiki, how are you?

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.769
-I'm good, how are you?

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.104
-I'm doing very well.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.739
I know you're based in
Los Angeles,

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.742
but is it true that
you made your way home

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:11.110
to get through these
troubled times?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.412
-Yes, I had to.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.648
I spent the first two months
of quarantine by myself,

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:19.652
and then I think I got tired
of myself.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.323
And so yeah, now I'm back here
in Cincinnati with family.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:27.260
-And now, have you managed
to not get tired of family?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.762
-You know, surprisingly we're
doing all right.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.164
[ Laughter ]
-All right.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.331
Good for you guys.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:33.599
-I'm like, we ain't
hanging in there.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:35.200
I think it's because
they're feeding me.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.772
So I'm like, as long as I get
free meals, I'm good.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.807
-And how has --
you know, obviously,

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.343
usually for a big movie
like this, you would be

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.810
traveling around and doing
a lot of press.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.647
Do you enjoy doing
a press junket from home?

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.183
-Um, yeah. I mean,
it has its benefits.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.817
It's pretty cool just,
you know, being able

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:53.686
to be at home doing this.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.489
But I don't know, I miss
some of the, you know, glam.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.292
[ Laughter ]
Some of the glam moments

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.560
have been a little
hard to let go of.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.930
But other than that, I'm like,
"This is pretty cool.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.998
We can keep doing this."
-Yeah.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.967
I imagine your family doesn't
lay out a nice thing

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.002
of croissants for you
every morning.

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:13.006
-Right, exactly. Maybe I should
ask them to do that.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.374
-Yeah.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.776
"The Old Guard" is such
a fun movie.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.812
It's based on a comic book
that I read and loved.

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.748
Greg Rucka who wrote it
wrote the screenplay.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:25.484
Did you know anything about this
comic going into it?

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:28.487
-No, I didn't know anything
about the comic until, you know,

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:30.289
I had started the
audition process.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.393
So that was my first
introduction to it.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.395
But I mean, once I read it,
I'm just like,

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:39.599
"Yo, this is dope. How do I get
to be a part of this?"

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:43.169
-And you got to work
with one of -- for my money

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.538
one of the dopest action stars
around right now,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.039
Charlize Theron.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:49.942
Did you -- I mean, I know she's
been injured a lot

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.343
doing stunts in her own films.

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:53.512
How did you hold up over the
course of the film

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:55.615
with a good amount
of fighting?

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.583
-Um, I held up pretty well.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.620
You know, I didn't get any,
I don't know, injuries

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.389
that would make me not want
to do it again.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.091
Just a few bumps and bruises.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.193
Which, I mean,
Charlize was actually

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.396
really helpful in giving me
some pointers in terms of

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.865
how to help heal
and take care of.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.635
And you know, any bumps
and bruises that were

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.237
a direct result of her,

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:21.674
I got some alcohol out of it,
some tequila, so.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.843
-Oh, so if Charlize
accidentally kicks you

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:26.812
or something, you'd get a bottle
of alcohol?

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.881
-Yeah, yeah.
So that, which I learned.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:31.684
I guess, I don't know if that's
like an action movie

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:35.754
kind of tradition, but
we were training, actually,

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:38.291
and she was wearing
her character boots

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.959
for the first time.
-Yes.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.963
-Threw a kick right at my shin.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:48.167
And out of that, I got me a very
nice sized bottle of tequila.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.903
I was like, "Okay."
-See, I would think

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.503
the more tequila you guys drank,

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:53.973
the more injuries would happen,
but maybe that's --

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.975
[ Laughter ]
Maybe that's part of the plan.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.343
-Right, I'm like,
maybe that's it.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.711
A little true.
A little true.

